From 2144592b32b07823e30b310ee89bee72cc9ffeb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:32:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(import): tessellate three-fillet corner blends
 instead of refusing them

The corner blend where three rounds meet is a rational patch with one side
collapsed to the corner vertex. Two faults kept a rounded-edge STEP from
importing:

- At the pole truck's parameter search returns the free parameter anywhere
  (-1.2e9 on the #1536 model, knot domain 0..1). truck then subdivides the
  bounding box of the boundary's parameters, a billion knot spans of
  extrapolation, which never converges: the #1536 hang, #1546's refusal.
  step_pole brings such an answer back inside the knot domain when the
  surface there is the same point.
- The rounded edges are SURFACE_CURVEs whose master is a pcurve. truck
  rebuilds them in its own parametrisation of the neighbouring surface, and
  every planar face lost a corner: the model imported at 13,981 mm3 of
  19,549.7 with no refusal. step_edge3d reads such an edge from its 3D
  curve directly (switching only the master makes truck invert a
  same_sense = .F. edge twice).

The #1536 model, rebuilt with solidcore (62 faces, 126 edges, 66 vertices),
now imports closed at 19,545.21 mm3 against the stated 19,549.71.

Pinned by import_step_corner_blend on testdata/models/fillet_corner.step
(one corner of that part) and by step_pole's unit tests.

Builds on #1546 (merged): its meter still bounds every face.

Fixes #1548

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
