From 820529a36cf1de35cecf602694abf4cc117fb3c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:45:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(import): refuse a STEP closed shell that meshes open,
 by name

truck drops a face it cannot place a boundary on, and mis-trims one it
places wrongly, without an error. A shell the file declares closed
(CLOSED_SHELL, or a MANIFOLD_SOLID_BREP's outer) whose kept mesh has
unmatched edges is now refused, naming the shell, its face count, the
unmatched-edge count, the first edge and any face the kernel gave no mesh;
a face with no mesh is refused in an open shell too.

Fixes #1573

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
